<hr data-start=3D"2209" data-end=3D"2212" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"2214" data-end=3D"2287" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2216" data-end=3D"2269">Chapitre 2 : L'Histoire de la Balise <code data-sta=
rt=3D"2255" data-end=3D"2267">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code></strong> (Interm=C3=
=A9diaire)</h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"2289" data-end=3D"2331" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2293" data-end=3D"2329">2.1 Les Origines du <code data-start=3D"2315" data-=
end=3D"2327">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code></strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2332" data-end=3D"2629" class=3D"">La balise <code data-st=
art=3D"2342" data-end=3D"2354">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> existe depuis les pr=
emi=C3=A8res versions du HTML.<br data-start=3D"2400" data-end=3D"2403">
Elle a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 introduite pour permettre aux navigateurs de savoir qu=
el type de document ils devaient rendre. Avant <strong data-start=3D"2515" =
data-end=3D"2524">HTML5</strong>, il y avait plusieurs versions du langage =
HTML, et chaque version avait sa propre d=C3=A9claration <code data-start=
=3D"2619" data-end=3D"2628">DOCTYPE</code>.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"2631" data-end=3D"2682" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2635" data-end=3D"2680">2.2 Les Types de <code data-start=3D"2654" data-end=
=3D"2666">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> avant HTML5</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"2683" data-end=3D"2778" class=3D"">Voici quelques exemples=
 de d=C3=A9clarations <code data-start=3D"2723" data-end=3D"2732">DOCTYPE</=
code> utilis=C3=A9es avant l'introduction de <strong data-start=3D"2767" da=
ta-end=3D"2776">HTML5</strong> :</p>
<h4 data-start=3D"2780" data-end=3D"2807" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
2785" data-end=3D"2805">HTML 4.01 Strict</strong></h4>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"2808" data-end=3D"2910"><div=
 class=3D"contain-inline-size rounded-md border-[0.5px] border-token-border=
