<p data-start=3D"3213" data-end=3D"3378" class=3D"">Chaque version de <code=
 data-start=3D"3231" data-end=3D"3240">DOCTYPE</code> =C3=A9tait associ=C3=
=A9e =C3=A0 un <strong data-start=3D"3261" data-end=3D"3295">Document Type =
Definition (DTD)</strong>, qui d=C3=A9finissait les r=C3=A8gles de syntaxe =
et les =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments autoris=C3=A9s dans un document.</p>
<h3 data-start=3D"3380" data-end=3D"3414" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3384" data-end=3D"3412">2.3 =C3=89volution vers HTML5</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"3415" data-end=3D"3750" class=3D"">Avec l=E2=80=99arriv=C3=
=A9e de <strong data-start=3D"3433" data-end=3D"3442">HTML5</strong>, la sy=
ntaxe <code data-start=3D"3455" data-end=3D"3472">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</co=
de> a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 simplifi=C3=A9e pour r=C3=A9pondre =C3=A0 un besoin de =
<strong data-start=3D"3519" data-end=3D"3548">compatibilit=C3=A9 universell=
e</strong>. Le but est de rendre le processus d'=C3=A9criture de HTML plus =
simple et plus clair. HTML5 =C3=A9tant une version plus souple et moderne, =
le <code data-start=3D"3681" data-end=3D"3690">DOCTYPE</code> a =C3=A9t=C3=
=A9 simplifi=C3=A9 et ne n=C3=A9cessite plus de r=C3=A9f=C3=A9rence =C3=A0 =
un DTD.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"3752" data-end=3D"3755" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"3757" data-end=3D"3820" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3759" data-end=3D"3809">Chapitre 3 : Le Fonctionnement de <code data-start=
=3D"3795" data-end=3D"3807">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code></strong> (Avanc=C3=A9)<=
/h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"3822" data-end=3D"3870" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
3826" data-end=3D"3868">3.1 Le Mode Quirks vs Le Mode Standard</strong></h3=
>
<p data-start=3D"3871" data-end=3D"3999" class=3D"">La d=C3=A9claration <co=
de data-start=3D"3886" data-end=3D"3898">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> indique au=
x navigateurs si le document doit =C3=AAtre rendu en <strong data-start=3D"=
3957" data-end=3D"3974">mode standard</strong> ou en <strong data-start=3D"=
3981" data-end=3D"3996">mode quirks</strong>.</p>
<ul data-start=3D"4000" data-end=3D"4391">
<li data-start=3D"4000" data-end=3D"4233" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4002" data-end=3D"4233" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
002" data-end=3D"4017">Mode Quirks</strong> : Un mode h=C3=A9ritage des anc=
iens navigateurs, o=C3=B9 certains comportements =C3=A9taient utilis=C3=A9s=
 pour assurer la compatibilit=C3=A9 avec des documents HTML plus anciens. C=
ela peut conduire =C3=A0 des bugs ou des comportements =C3=A9tranges.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4234" data-end=3D"4391" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4236" data-end=3D"4391" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
236" data-end=3D"4253">Mode Standard</strong> : Le navigateur rend la page =
conform=C3=A9ment aux normes modernes, en utilisant le mod=C3=A8le de bo=C3=
=AEte, le CSS et le JavaScript les plus r=C3=A9cents.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"4393" data-end=3D"4452" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4397" data-end=3D"4450">3.2 Que fait la balise <code data-start=3D"4422" da=
ta-end=3D"4434">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> en pratique ?</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4453" data-end=3D"4512" class=3D"">Lorsqu'un navigateur re=
ncontre la balise <code data-start=3D"4494" data-end=3D"4506">&lt;!DOCTYPE&=
gt;</code>, il :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"4513" data-end=3D"4793">
<li data-start=3D"4513" data-end=3D"4572" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4516" data-end=3D"4572" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
516" data-end=3D"4527">V=C3=A9rifie</strong> quel type de document il est c=
ens=C3=A9 afficher.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4573" data-end=3D"4711" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4576" data-end=3D"4711" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
576" data-end=3D"4603">Active le mode standard</strong> s=E2=80=99il trouve=
 une d=C3=A9claration valide, ou active le mode quirks si la d=C3=A9clarati=
on est manquante ou incorrecte.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"4712" data-end=3D"4793" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"4715" data-end=3D"4793" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"4=
715" data-end=3D"4731">Rend la page</strong> en respectant les r=C3=A8gles =
d=C3=A9finies pour ce type de document.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-start=3D"4795" data-end=3D"4843" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
4799" data-end=3D"4841">3.3 Le <code data-start=3D"4808" data-end=3D"4820">=
&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> et les Navigateurs</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"4844" data-end=3D"5188" class=3D"">Tous les navigateurs mo=
dernes (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge) respectent la d=C3=A9claration <code=
 data-start=3D"4932" data-end=3D"4944">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code>. Cependant, =
certains anciens navigateurs (comme <strong data-start=3D"4993" data-end=3D=
"5020">Internet Explorer 6 =C3=A0 8</strong>) avaient un comportement diff=
=C3=A9rent selon le type de <code data-start=3D"5073" data-end=3D"5082">DOC=
TYPE</code> utilis=C3=A9. L=E2=80=99absence de <code data-start=3D"5105" da=
ta-end=3D"5114">DOCTYPE</code> ou une d=C3=A9claration incorrecte pouvait e=
ntra=C3=AEner des erreurs d'affichage.</p>
<hr data-start=3D"5190" data-end=3D"5193" class=3D"">
<h1 data-start=3D"5195" data-end=3D"5258" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5197" data-end=3D"5247">Chapitre 4 : La Balise <code data-start=3D"5222" da=
ta-end=3D"5234">&lt;!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> avec HTML5</strong> (Expert)</h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"5260" data-end=3D"5295" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
5264" data-end=3D"5293">4.1 Le <code data-start=3D"5273" data-end=3D"5282">=
DOCTYPE</code> en HTML5</strong></h3>
<p data-start=3D"5296" data-end=3D"5466" class=3D"">HTML5 a simplifi=C3=A9 =
l'utilisation de la balise <code data-start=3D"5341" data-end=3D"5353">&lt;=
!DOCTYPE&gt;</code> en =C3=A9liminant la n=C3=A9cessit=C3=A9 de se r=C3=A9f=
=C3=A9rer =C3=A0 un DTD externe. La syntaxe a =C3=A9t=C3=A9 r=C3=A9duite =
=C3=A0 la forme la plus simple :</p>
