<h3 data-start=3D"4902" data-end=3D"4944" class=3D"">3.2 Le mod=C3=A8le de =
bo=C3=AEte CSS (Box Model)</h3>
<p data-start=3D"4946" data-end=3D"5106" class=3D"">Le <strong data-start=
=3D"4949" data-end=3D"4968">mod=C3=A8le de bo=C3=AEte</strong> CSS est esse=
ntiel pour comprendre la mani=C3=A8re dont les =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments HTML sont=
 affich=C3=A9s. Chaque =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment a une bo=C3=AEte rectangulaire com=
pos=C3=A9e de :</p>
<ul data-start=3D"5107" data-end=3D"5282">
<li data-start=3D"5107" data-end=3D"5143" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5109" data-end=3D"5143" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
109" data-end=3D"5120">Contenu</strong> (textes, images, etc.)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5144" data-end=3D"5184" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5146" data-end=3D"5184" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
146" data-end=3D"5157">Padding</strong> (espace autour du contenu)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5185" data-end=3D"5240" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5187" data-end=3D"5240" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
187" data-end=3D"5198">Bordure</strong> (bordure autour du contenu et du pa=
dding)</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"5241" data-end=3D"5282" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"5243" data-end=3D"5282" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"5=
243" data-end=3D"5252">Marge</strong> (espace autour de la bordure)</p>
</li>
</ul>
