<h2 data-start=3D"95" data-end=3D"147" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"98"=
 data-end=3D"145">Introduction aux S=C3=A9lecteurs Combin=C3=A9s en CSS</st=
rong></h2>
<p data-start=3D"149" data-end=3D"391" class=3D"">Les <strong data-start=3D=
"153" data-end=3D"176">s=C3=A9lecteurs combin=C3=A9s</strong> permettent de=
 cibler des =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments HTML en fonction de leurs relations avec d=
=E2=80=99autres =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments. Cela permet d=E2=80=99affiner le ciblag=
e et d=E2=80=99appliquer des styles uniquement =C3=A0 certains =C3=A9l=C3=
=A9ments d=E2=80=99une structure HTML donn=C3=A9e.</p>
<p data-start=3D"393" data-end=3D"461" class=3D"">Il existe trois principau=
x types de <strong data-start=3D"429" data-end=3D"452">s=C3=A9lecteurs comb=
in=C3=A9s</strong> en CSS :</p>
<ol data-start=3D"463" data-end=3D"660">
<li data-start=3D"463" data-end=3D"517" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"466" data-end=3D"517" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"466=
" data-end=3D"515">Le s=C3=A9lecteur descendant (<code data-start=3D"493" d=
ata-end=3D"512">=C3=A9l=C3=A9mentA =C3=A9l=C3=A9mentB</code>)</strong></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"518" data-end=3D"577" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"521" data-end=3D"577" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"521=
" data-end=3D"575">Le s=C3=A9lecteur enfant direct (<code data-start=3D"551=
" data-end=3D"572">=C3=A9l=C3=A9mentA &gt; =C3=A9l=C3=A9mentB</code>)</stro=
ng></p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"578" data-end=3D"660" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"581" data-end=3D"660" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"581=
" data-end=3D"658">Les s=C3=A9lecteurs de fr=C3=A8res (<code data-start=3D"=
609" data-end=3D"630">=C3=A9l=C3=A9mentA + =C3=A9l=C3=A9mentB</code> et <co=
de data-start=3D"634" data-end=3D"655">=C3=A9l=C3=A9mentA ~ =C3=A9l=C3=A9me=
ntB</code>)</strong></p>
</li>
</ol>
<p data-start=3D"662" data-end=3D"785" class=3D"">Dans ce tutoriel, nous al=
lons examiner chacun de ces s=C3=A9lecteurs en d=C3=A9tail, avec des explic=
