></h1>
<h3 data-start=3D"6690" data-end=3D"6711" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
6694" data-end=3D"6711">Limitations :</strong></h3>
<ul data-start=3D"6712" data-end=3D"7279">
<li data-start=3D"6712" data-end=3D"6901" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6714" data-end=3D"6901" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
714" data-end=3D"6743">Support des navigateurs :</strong> Bien que la plupa=
rt des navigateurs modernes supportent <code data-start=3D"6800" data-end=
=3D"6818">position: sticky</code>, certains navigateurs plus anciens (comme=
 Internet Explorer) ne le supportent pas.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"6902" data-end=3D"7091" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"6904" data-end=3D"7091" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"6=
904" data-end=3D"6940">Parent avec <code data-start=3D"6918" data-end=3D"69=
36">overflow: hidden</code> :</strong> Si un =C3=A9l=C3=A9ment sticky est c=
ontenu dans un parent ayant <code data-start=3D"6995" data-end=3D"7013">ove=
rflow: hidden</code>, il ne deviendra pas sticky, car il sera limit=C3=A9 p=
ar le contexte du conteneur.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"7092" data-end=3D"7279" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"7094" data-end=3D"7279" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"7=
094" data-end=3D"7133">Contexte d'empilement (<code data-start=3D"7119" dat=
a-end=3D"7128">z-index</code>) :</strong> Comme <code data-start=3D"7140" d=
ata-end=3D"7148">sticky</code> est un type de positionnement qui sort du fl=
ux normal, vous devrez g=C3=A9rer les <code data-start=3D"7226" data-end=3D=
"7235">z-index</code> pour =C3=A9viter les probl=C3=A8mes de superposition.=
</p>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 data-start=3D"7281" data-end=3D"7307" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"=
7285" data-end=3D"7307">Bonnes pratiques :</strong></h3>
