<li data-start=3D"1151" data-end=3D"1211" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1153" data-end=3D"1211" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
153" data-end=3D"1174">Les =C3=A9l=C3=A9ments HTML</strong> deviennent des =
n=C5=93uds dans cet arbre.</p>
</li>
<li data-start=3D"1212" data-end=3D"1294" class=3D"">
<p data-start=3D"1214" data-end=3D"1294" class=3D""><strong data-start=3D"1=
214" data-end=3D"1234">Les balises HTML</strong> deviennent des objets Java=
Script que vous pouvez manipuler.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p data-start=3D"1296" data-end=3D"1382" class=3D"">Par exemple, voici un p=
etit extrait de code HTML qui repr=C3=A9sente une structure simple :</p>
<pre class=3D"!overflow-visible" data-start=3D"1384" data-end=3D"1676"><div=
